<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Archive of the Crown of Aragon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1318</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Arxiu de la Corona d'Aragó</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Archive of the Crown of Aragon in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> is one of the oldest and richest archives in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. It grew from the royal archive organised by King James II in 1318 and holds records of the counts of Barcelona and kings of Aragon from the ninth century onwards, with documents on the Crown's realms and interests across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/archive-of-the-crown-of-aragon.jpg" alt="Archive of the Crown of Aragon" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jaume Meneses · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Exterior_Palau_del_Lloctinent.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
